bal:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"One unnecessary bounded mutation occurred: the malformed compound verification in cmd-a7bd89038925482f left a test sleep process and its background shell running after the useful live-stop portion. Both were explicitly killed by cmd-8ad72f8792c343f4, and no final residue is evident. Other mutations had clear implementation, verification, restart-protocol, or cleanup roles. Final snapshots show no failed services, package damage, added listeners, or abnormal temporary-file residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a7bd89038925482f","cmd-f48fa76ae631434d","cmd-8ad72f8792c343f4","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The final provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state, an acknowledged restart, a changed boot identity, persisted configuration and journal data, and successful stale-PID recovery to one healthy worker. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently confirm that the node restarted.","limitations":["Foreign-PID start/stop behavior was directly tested immediately before the final edit; the last edit only redirected a transient /proc read error, and final post-edit testing covered stop/start/status, stale recovery, and singleton behavior but did not repeat the complete foreign-PID sequence.","The lifecycle snapshots provide host-level hygiene observations but do not inventory every file under the repaired application directory; application state is instead supported by direct executor evidence and the authored baseline."]}
